# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to .env and fill in. Nothing here is a real credential.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser bundle, and
# everything it does expose is readable by anyone who loads the app. Treat the
# key below as public: lock it down with an Alchemy domain allowlist rather
# than relying on it staying secret.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Alchemy API key for Arc Testnet (chain id 5042002).
#
# This is the load-bearing setting. The public endpoint at
# https://rpc.testnet.arc.network answers fine from curl, but returns no
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin header and 400s the OPTIONS preflight — so from a
# browser every eth_call fails with net::ERR_FAILED before it leaves the tab,
# and search, records and prices all render as if nothing exists. Alchemy
# echoes the requesting origin back, so it works from the browser.
VITE_ALCHEMY_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY_HERE

# Full RPC URL. Overrides VITE_ALCHEMY_API_KEY when set — use it to point at a
# self-hosted node or a CORS-enabled proxy. Must be CORS-enabled for the origin
# the app is served from.
# VITE_ARC_RPC_URL=https://arc-testnet.g.alchemy.com/v2/YOUR_API_KEY_HERE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WalletConnect. Free project ID from https://cloud.reown.com
#
# Unset, the connect modal degrades to offering only installed browser
# extensions — every WalletConnect-backed wallet is hidden rather than failing
# at connect time with an opaque error. That also removes the only way to
# connect from a phone browser without an in-app wallet, so set this before
# deploying anywhere mobile users will find it. Local dev works without it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=YOUR_PROJECT_ID_HERE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Indexer API. Left unset, the app uses same-origin /api/v1/* paths, which the
# Vite dev server proxies to INDEXER_ORIGIN (default http://localhost:8787).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_INDEXER_API_URL=http://localhost:8787

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which site this build serves: `app` (default) or `waitlist`.
#
# Normally you do not set this. One deployment serves both hosts and picks by
# hostname — anything under `join.` renders the standalone mainnet waitlist,
# everything else renders the app. Two Vercel domains, one project, one bundle.
#
# The override exists for the two cases a hostname cannot answer: local
# development (everything is `localhost`) and Vercel preview URLs (`*.vercel.app`,
# with no `join.` label). Set it to `waitlist` to work on the signup flow.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_SITE_MODE=waitlist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contract overrides. All optional — the deployed proxy addresses are compiled
# in as defaults (see src/config/contracts.ts). Only set these against a fresh
# deployment, and only ever to a proxy address, never an implementation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_REGISTRY_ADDRESS=0xCA78696791670CbC14eE802e6DcDfD661a458978
# VITE_REGISTRAR_ADDRESS=0x3dC38247c4f9672B2C98aCfdc5C1302f8d897E9C
# VITE_RESOLVER_ADDRESS=0x027d6dCc8F1235dfdd47E532e77909363C701E54
# VITE_CONTROLLER_ADDRESS=0x2FE2560B2FE6D54e50806F531223247CcfEd739B
# VITE_MARKET_ADDRESS=0xC94Ff1964840BdF8E6952455a2342Ffc6B0bA299
# VITE_UNIVERSAL_RESOLVER_ADDRESS=0xA3F364a558eb712AFbB4929df49e538A800438BC
# VITE_REVERSE_REGISTRAR_ADDRESS=0x97cdcf037c1A8475eF5C9504A18C10b41f7DfDfB
